\id JHN Sidebars — authored for this repository
\c 1
\p
\v 1 A sidebar interrupts the body without belonging to it. Everything between
\esb and \esbe is a separate flow, and a renderer that treats it as body text
puts an essay in the middle of a verse.
\esb \cat History\cat*
\ms Weights and Measures
\p A sidebar carries its own paragraph structure, and its own headings.
\p It may also carry a category, which is what a publisher filters on when
deciding which sidebars a given edition includes.
\esbe
\v 2 The body resumes here, and the verse that was interrupted must still read
as one verse.
\p
\v 3 Sidebars nest nothing, but they do contain most things.
\esb
\p A sidebar with no category at all.
\li1 Including lists,
\li2 nested ones,
\q1 poetry,
\q2 and its indents.
\esbe
\v 4 A sidebar left unclosed at the end of a chapter is a diagnostic rather
than a parse failure.
\esb \cat Deuterocanon\cat*
\p This one never closes.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 And the next chapter begins anyway.
